WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:03.903
There are three kinds of
donuts, sugary ring donuts,

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:07.240
sugary jelly-filled donuts, and
then there are the ones that

00:00:07.307 --> 00:00:10.210
are really bad for your health.

00:00:10.276 --> 00:00:13.213
These ones.

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.749
Well, I can see why people
pay money to watch this.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:21.354
But take any friction
fighting hijinks to the roads

00:00:21.421 --> 00:00:30.029
and it's a serious hazard
for motorists and for trees.

00:00:30.096 --> 00:00:32.999
They were okay, but
extremely lucky.

00:00:33.066 --> 00:00:34.701
So you should
never attempt this.

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.003
But off the road, and in
the hands of an expert,

00:00:37.070 --> 00:00:42.642
donuts are a masterclass in
static and kinetic friction.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:47.580
Our driver hits the gas
hard and turns sharply.

00:00:47.647 --> 00:00:49.616
The excessive torque
at the rear wheels

00:00:49.682 --> 00:00:53.019
overcome static friction between
the tires and the ground,

00:00:53.086 --> 00:00:55.355
so they become subject
to kinetic friction,

00:00:55.422 --> 00:00:56.656
which offers less resistance.

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.327
The reduced grip allows
centrifugal force

00:01:01.394 --> 00:01:04.097
to slide the wheels
in a circular path,

00:01:04.164 --> 00:01:05.165
like the ring of a donut.

00:01:09.002 --> 00:01:11.404
So not just risky,
but scientifically

00:01:11.471 --> 00:01:16.810
tricky to pull off, although
not everyone seems to think so.

00:01:16.876 --> 00:01:18.912
I mean this guy thinks
he's got the science down,

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:21.748
but in fact he hasn't lost
traction at his back tires

00:01:21.815 --> 00:01:24.184
at all.

00:01:24.250 --> 00:01:27.720
He's just using rollers, see,
which does reduce the risk

00:01:27.787 --> 00:01:31.624
of kinetic friction,
burning up the tires,

00:01:31.691 --> 00:01:33.793
but doesn't make
it less dangerous.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:34.594
CAMERA MAN: Woah!

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:36.362
Watch out, man!

00:01:36.429 --> 00:01:39.098
BEN AARON: It's a
bit late for that.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:42.569
Ah, the parking lot donut,
using kinetic friction

00:01:42.635 --> 00:01:50.443
and centrifugal force to drift
into a space, like a glove.

00:01:50.510 --> 00:01:52.479
Having successfully
turned static friction

00:01:52.545 --> 00:01:56.449
to kinetic at the
rear wheels, he then

00:01:56.516 --> 00:01:58.852
momentarily let up the
power on those wheels

00:01:58.918 --> 00:02:00.954
and went back to static.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:03.756
So, he stopped circling,
and went straight.

00:02:06.693 --> 00:02:08.962
There are better
ways to park a car.

